{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.KnotTheory","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.KnotTheory","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Basic","lean:module:QOU.Glossary","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":45,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.writhe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.writhe","kind":"def","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory.lean#L210-L222","doc":"The writhe of a braid word (signed sum of exponents).\nFor a braid word `σ_{i_1}^{ε_1} ⋯ σ_{i_k}^{ε_k}`, this returns\n`ε_1 + ⋯ + ε_k`.  Note: this is the *braid-projection writhe*; it\ncounts crossings *between strands* with signs.  Per-component\nself-writhe (counted only within a single component of the\nclosure) is zero in the standard braid projection — strands do\nnot self-cross. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.vol_trefoil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.vol_trefoil","kind":"def","line":202,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory.lean#L202-L206","doc":"The trefoil is a torus knot and has zero hyperbolic volume. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.vol_figure_eight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.vol_figure_eight","kind":"def","line":192,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory.lean#L192-L200","doc":"The hyperbolic volume of the figure-eight knot (4₁).\nExact: 3 · Cl₂(π/3) where Cl₂ is the Clausen function.\nValue: 2.029883212819307250042405 (OEIS A091518, 24 dps verified;\nprevious 15-dps literal `2.02988321281931 ± 1×10⁻¹⁴` bumped\n2026-06-07). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.writhe_borromeanRings","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.writhe_borromeanRings","kind":"theorem","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory.lean#L185-L188","doc":"The Borromean rings `(σ_0 σ_1^{-1})^3` have writhe `0`, matching\n`QOU.StandardModel.WritheMarkovInvariance.writhe_borromean` on the\n`List ℤ` encoding of the same word. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.writhe_hopfLink","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.writhe_hopfLink","kind":"theorem","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory.lean#L182-L183","doc":"The Hopf link `σ_0^2` has writhe `+2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.writhe_figureEight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.writhe_figureEight","kind":"theorem","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory.lean#L177-L180","doc":"The figure-eight `(σ_0 σ_1^{-1})^2` has writhe `0`: the alternating\nword cancels, so writhe does **not** separate it from the unknot —\nthe crossing count does. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.writhe_trefoil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.writhe_trefoil","kind":"theorem","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory.lean#L173-L175","doc":"The trefoil `σ_0^3` has writhe `+3` — all three crossings positive,\nso the bound `|w| ≤ c` of `abs_writhe_le_crossingCount` is tight. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.writhe_unknot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.writhe_unknot","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory.lean#L170-L171","doc":"The unknot has writhe `0` (empty word). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.borromeanRings","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.borromeanRings","kind":"def","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory.lean#L153-L163","doc":"The Borromean rings (L6a4) — closed braid `(σ_0 σ_1^{-1})^3` in\n`B_3`, 3 components.  In the QOU framework, the Borromean rings\nare the nucleon (three quark strands, Brunnian linking). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.hopfLink","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.hopfLink","kind":"def","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory.lean#L144-L151","doc":"The Hopf link (L2a1) — closed braid `σ_0^2` in `B_2`, 2 components.\nIn the QOU framework, the Hopf link is the gluon / strong force\nbinding. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.figureEight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.figureEight","kind":"def","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory.lean#L134-L142","doc":"The figure-eight knot (4₁) — closed braid `(σ_0 σ_1^{-1})^2` in\n`B_3`.  In the QOU framework, the figure-eight maps to the muon. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.trefoil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.trefoil","kind":"def","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory.lean#L126-L132","doc":"The trefoil knot (3₁) — closed braid `σ_0^3` in `B_2`.\nIn the QOU framework, the trefoil maps to the electron. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.unknot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.unknot","kind":"def","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory.lean#L119-L124","doc":"The unknot — empty braid word in `B_1` (1 strand, 0 crossings). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.HyperbolicVolume.error_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.HyperbolicVolume.error_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory.lean#L115-L115","doc":"Proof obligation: error bound is non-negative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.HyperbolicVolume.error_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.HyperbolicVolume.error_bound","kind":"def","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory.lean#L112-L112","doc":"Error bound (half-width of confidence interval). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.HyperbolicVolume.value","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.HyperbolicVolume.value","kind":"def","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory.lean#L110-L110","doc":"The volume value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.HyperbolicVolume.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.HyperbolicVolume.mk","kind":"ctor","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory.lean#L108-L108","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.HyperbolicVolume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.HyperbolicVolume","kind":"structure","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory.lean#L107-L115","doc":"Hyperbolic volume of a knot complement, with error bound. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.BraidWord.abs_writhe_le_crossingCount","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.BraidWord.abs_writhe_le_crossingCount","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory.lean#L89-L103","doc":"`|w(β)| ≤ c(β)`: the writhe is bounded by the crossing count,\nwith equality iff every letter has the same sign.  Each summand\ncontributes `±1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.BraidWord.writhe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.BraidWord.writhe","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory.lean#L77-L87","doc":"**Writhe** of a braid word: the exponent sum\n`w(β) = Σ_j ε_j` over its letters `σ_{i_j}^{ε_j}`.\n\nThis is the writhe of the Markov closure diagram, and is the\n`O(n)` computation this file's header promises alongside\n`crossingCount`.  Unlike the crossing count it is signed, so it\nis not a knot invariant on its own — it changes under Markov\nstabilisation — but it is exactly the framing correction that\nturns the Ocneanu trace into a link invariant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.BraidLetter.signValue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.BraidLetter.signValue","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory.lean#L74-L75","doc":"The signed value of a braid letter `σ_i^ε`, i.e. its exponent `ε`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.CrossingSign.value","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.CrossingSign.value","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory.lean#L68-L72","doc":"The integer value of a crossing sign: `+1` for `σ_i`, `-1` for\n`σ_i^{-1}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.BraidWord.crossingCount","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.BraidWord.crossingCount","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory.lean#L64-L66","doc":"Number of crossings = length of the braid word. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.instReprBraidWord.repr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.instReprBraidWord.repr","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory.lean#L62-L62","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.instReprBraidWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.instReprBraidWord","kind":"instance","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory.lean#L62-L62","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.BraidWord.components","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.BraidWord.components","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory.lean#L61-L61","doc":"Number of components in the Markov closure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.BraidWord.letters","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.BraidWord.letters","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory.lean#L59-L59","doc":"Sequence of generator letters applied left-to-right. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.BraidWord.strands","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.BraidWord.strands","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory.lean#L57-L57","doc":"Number of strands `n` for the ambient braid group `B_n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.BraidWord.name","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.BraidWord.name","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory.lean#L55-L55","doc":"Alexander–Briggs name or other identifier (e.g. `\"3_1\"`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.BraidWord.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.BraidWord.mk","kind":"ctor","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory.lean#L53-L53","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.BraidWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.BraidWord","kind":"structure","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory.lean#L51-L62","doc":"A braid word in `B_n` together with the Markov closure data needed\nto recover a knot or link. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.instDecidableEqBraidLetter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.instDecidableEqBraidLetter","kind":"instance","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory.lean#L47-L47","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.instDecidableEqBraidLetter.decEq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.instDecidableEqBraidLetter.decEq","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory.lean#L47-L47","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.instReprBraidLetter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.instReprBraidLetter","kind":"instance","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory.lean#L47-L47","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.instReprBraidLetter.repr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.instReprBraidLetter.repr","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory.lean#L47-L47","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.BraidLetter.sign","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.BraidLetter.sign","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory.lean#L46-L46","doc":"Exponent sign: positive = `σ_i`, negative = `σ_i^{-1}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.BraidLetter.index","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.BraidLetter.index","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory.lean#L44-L44","doc":"Generator index: `i` in `σ_i`. Valid in `B_n` when `i + 1 < n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.BraidLetter.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.BraidLetter.mk","kind":"ctor","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory.lean#L42-L42","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.BraidLetter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.BraidLetter","kind":"structure","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory.lean#L39-L47","doc":"A single braid-generator letter `σ_i^ε`: index `i` says which\nadjacent pair of strands crosses; `sign` says positive or negative\nexponent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.instReprCrossingSign.repr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.instReprCrossingSign.repr","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory.lean#L37-L37","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.instReprCrossingSign","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.instReprCrossingSign","kind":"instance","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory.lean#L37-L37","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.instDecidableEqCrossingSign","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.instDecidableEqCrossingSign","kind":"instance","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory.lean#L37-L37","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.CrossingSign.negative","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.CrossingSign.negative","kind":"ctor","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory.lean#L36-L36","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.CrossingSign.positive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.CrossingSign.positive","kind":"ctor","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory.lean#L35-L35","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.CrossingSign","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.CrossingSign","kind":"inductive","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory.lean#L33-L37","doc":"The exponent sign of a braid generator: `σ_i^{+1}` or `σ_i^{-1}`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}